From: j7 fb
Subject: j7 fb: hand clients a canvas surface of their own

Selector 3 handed out a view of the scanout buffer, so CoreAnimation rendered half its
frames into panel memory at canvas size: those landed unscaled in the top-left corner and
present() skipped them, which is the flicker between a scaled frame and a raw 750-wide one.

The first attempt at this allocated a buffer and published a surface over its physical
address. That maps one page twice, once cacheable and once write-combined, and it panicked
in pmap_enter_pv (unexpected PV head) on 2026-11-14. Allocate the pixels through the surface
subsystem itself instead - one mapping, shared once, the same path a client create uses.

The first eight swap records also print their layer mask and four layer ids now, so a log
says whether a wallpaper layer exists and what to composite under the UI.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.h b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.h
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.h
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.h
@@ -66,6 +66,15 @@
 SweetSurface *sweet_surface_create_physical_len(uint64_t phys, uint32_t width,
     uint32_t height, uint32_t bytesPerRow, uint32_t pixelFormat, uint32_t mappedHeight);
 
+/*
+ * A surface over memory the kernel allocates and shares: what a client-facing
+ * surface must be. Do not build one by mapping a buffer a second time at a
+ * different cache mode - two mappings of one physical page with different
+ * attributes corrupt the pmap PV lists (pmap_enter_pv, 2026-11-14).
+ */
+SweetSurface *sweet_surface_create_owned(uint32_t width, uint32_t height,
+    uint32_t bytesPerRow, uint32_t pixelFormat);
+
 /* Send right for the surface in task (IOSurfaceLookupFromMachPort). */
 mach_port_name_t sweet_surface_port_in_task(SweetSurface *surface, task_t task);
 
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetSurface.cpp
@@ -265,6 +265,39 @@
 	    height);
 }
 
+SweetSurface *
+sweet_surface_create_owned(uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t bytesPerRow,
+    uint32_t pixelFormat)
+{
+	SweetSurface *s = sweet_surface_alloc();
+	IOBufferMemoryDescriptor *mem;
+
+	if (s == NULL) {
+		return NULL;
+	}
+	s->width = width;
+	s->height = height;
+	s->bytesPerRow = bytesPerRow;
+	s->bytesPerElement = 4;
+	s->elementWidth = s->elementHeight = 1;
+	s->pixelFormat = pixelFormat;
+	s->allocSize = (uint32_t)round_page((uint64_t)bytesPerRow * height);
+	mem = IOBufferMemoryDescriptor::inTaskWithOptions(kernel_task,
+	    kIODirectionInOut | kIOMemoryKernelUserShared, s->allocSize, page_size);
+	if (mem == NULL) {
+		s->release();
+		return NULL;
+	}
+	bzero(mem->getBytesNoCopy(), s->allocSize);
+	s->memory = mem;
+	s->mapCache = kIOMapDefaultCache;
+	if (!sweet_surface_publish(s)) {
+		s->release();
+		return NULL;
+	}
+	return s;
+}
+
 mach_port_name_t
 sweet_surface_port_in_task(SweetSurface *s, task_t task)
 {
